Changes in v6:
- drop WARN_ON() on ibmveth_toggle_irq() returns; the helper already
  logs the hcall rc, and rate-limit that print
- remask+sync all queues on setup_rx enable-fail unwind, including
  queue i (fix while (--i) rollback; err_disable_napi mirrors
  cleanup remask)
- reword schedule_rx_queue() kdoc — true means NAPI scheduled (mask
  attempted); disable_irq failure is logged by the helper and does not
  change the return.
  Out-of-range qindex WARN returns false (not a prep failure). Keep
  mask-only-on-prep-success; do not mask when prep fails.
- open fail without h_free_logical_lan on pool-fail predates this IRQ
  patch (LAN registered before buffer pools). The opened gate here
  removes the accidental h_free recovery a later ndo_stop used to
  provide after failed reopen. Series tip already fixes ordering in
  P06 (h_free before pool DMA on open-fail) and P07 (pools before
  register_rx_queues; post-register errors funnel through
  free_all_queues). No further change on P05.
- no standalone Fixes: tag (opened-gate hang named above; not
  backportable without this IRQ refactor).
- early !opened close can skip TX LTB free only when set_channels
  allocates while the adapter is closed (v5 keyed on IFF_UP after failed
  reopen). Series tip gates set_channels on opened in P14; P15
  publishes RX count and CMO while down and does not allocate TX
  LTBs or wake queues. close still frees TX LTB when opened had
  been true. No change in this IRQ patch.
- per-queue poll completion and enable_irq(qindex) in P09 before P10;
  IRQ handler uses &napi[i] cookie at SQ (only napi[0] registered here)

Changes in v5:
- Remask+sync after napi_disable in cleanup (in-flight poll can re-arm)
- Interrupt: quiet IRQ_NONE on out-of-range qindex (no WARN storm)
- Opened / rx_irq_setup gate cleanup so close after a failed open
  cannot napi_disable / free_irq without a prior enable/request; set
  opened on successful open; rx_irq_setup only on full setup success
- H_PARAMETER fold disable-only; enable stays error (stuck-masked visible)
- IRQ helpers return 0 / negative errno only (never raw H_* to ethtool)
- Decision: keep open IRQ order request_irq -> napi_enable while PHYP
  stays masked until schedule/enable (coherent with later scale-up)
- schedule_rx_queue returns bool (napi_schedule_prep success)
- Keep mask-only-on-prep-success (no else-mask; avoids idle+masked race)
- Call out free_irq-before-free_lan as intentional once PHYP is masked
- Poll re-arm during teardown lands with SQ poll-harden (not claimed here)
- synchronize_net() after RX IRQ/NAPI teardown in close
- Add subordinate IRQ dispose helpers (per-queue + bulk 1..N; bound to MAX)
